The spread campaign is closed. Both of the owner's answers are applied, and the final case table is in `docs/spread_cases.md`. Nothing ran on the GPUs this wake.

## What the owner decided
- **No more training.** The control run (the tail layout trained with the same single extra training pass the spread model got, about 44–60 GPU-hours) is not run. Spread stays the base layout, and the GPU time goes to the stage-2 rebuild (the next round of the second training stage).
- **Scoring rule.** A case counts as "better" when the rubric judge, the project prompt and exact match all say better. Its size range is reported next to it.
- **One mismatch.** The question file had recommended option A (train the control), but the relayed answer said "do as recommended" and named option C. I did option C, as written. I logged this as a tooling gap, because the loop can't tell a relay slip from a real choice.

## Final answer: spread layout vs tail layout
Judge accuracy (share of answers the judge marks correct, higher is better), paired on the same 1,500 questions, two seeds. Every row uses 8 tokens per compressed slot.

| Case | Spread − tail | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| 10 HotpotQA passages compressed as one chunk | +25 to +27 pt (judges), +15 pt (exact match) | **better** |
| One long MRQA passage | +7 to +10 pt (judges), +6 to +7 pt (exact match) | **better** |
| Photos | +0.1 pt pooled | **equal** under the rubric judge and exact match, not certified under the project prompt |
| 10 HotpotQA passages as 10 chunks | judges tie; exact match favours tail by 2 pt | tie, but the verdict changes with the scoring |
| Documents, 4 pages | +1.7 pt (95% interval −0.2 to +3.6) | cannot be decided with this set |
| Documents, 10 or 20 pages | the gap does not grow with more pages | — |

Still open: spread's +8–9 pt document gain at the small training budget disappears at the full budget, and we don't know why. One possible reason: the tail models had three extra training passes against one for spread. Only the control run could test that, and it is now not run.

## Done this wake
- I rewrote the case table, the state file and the results page as final.
- The retro is written and the campaign is on stand-down, so later cron ticks do nothing.
- I sent a hand-off to the pisco chat: apply the final wording to `docs/architecture_review.md:252-256` and to thread 1 of `HANDOFF.md`. The text is in `campaign_spread/STATE.md`.

Your decision: whenever convenient, paste `campaign_spread/SYNC.md` into `~/.claude/SYNC.md` and run `expmon campaign disarm` to remove the cron line. If you really meant option A (train the control), say so and the campaign can be re-armed.
